            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F001:F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"In F006, the text explicitly specifies that 'Subparagraph (A) shall not apply with respect to the filing of an action by an attorney general of a State under this subsection, if the attorney general determines that it is not feasible to provide the notice described in that subparagraph before the filing of the action.' Subparagraph (A) corresponds directly to claim C0000. Therefore, establishing C0001 as an exception qualifying C0000 is directly supported by the text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F006:F009\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"C0001 explicitly exempts the attorney general from Subparagraph (A) (represented by C0000), not clause (ii) (represented by C0002). Instead, C0002 imposes an affirmative duty in actions described in clause (i) (C0001). Therefore, C0001 does not serve as an exception qualifying C0002.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
